<p>The rendering stage dominates latency. For sites that require JavaScript rendering, the P95 latency of 9.3 seconds means a pipeline processing 10,000 products can expect to take about 26 hours if all pages require rendering. Using a rendering decision cache — where the pipeline remembers which sites need rendering and skips the browser for sites that do not — cuts total runtime by approximately 60%.</p>

